{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5RRKgBhfNCn3hpK63a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed, and `tests/test_resolver.py` passes (36 tests).\n\n`find_all_matching_from_provider` in `src/fromager/resolver.py` now skips the `--max-release-age` filter for any package that has a constraint. It logs `constrained by <spec>, skipping max release age filter` and returns every candidate the constraint allows. That fixes both reported symptoms:\n- **Multi-version mode:** a pinned package like `boto3==1.35.88` no longer ends up with an empty candidate list and a silent resolution failure.\n- **Single-version mode:** the misleading \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning no longer appears for pinned packages.\n\nI added three regression tests to `tests/test_resolver.py`:\n- **Pinned, fallback on and off:** a pinned package with only old candidates keeps all of them, with no \"keeping all\" warning.\n- **Unconstrained, fallback off:** the same package without a constraint still gets an empty list, so the age filter itself is unchanged.\n\nI only ran `tests/test_resolver.py`, not the full suite, lint or mypy. I haven't committed anything.\n\nThe skip applies to any constraint on the package, not only an exact `==` pin. A range like `boto3>=1.35` would also bypass the age filter. I treated any constraint as explicit user intent; say so if you want it limited to exact pins."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9162,"cache_read_input_tokens":89125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9162},"output_tokens":455,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62e78071-0c12-4ac4-88de-e6f32b974e6c","uuid":"f790b505-a0df-40d7-bf78-a62b8f69eacc","times